They are possible TARGETS.

Do not add autonomous drones/robots yet.

==================================================
8. TARGET CONTRACT
==================================================

Reuse M14.4.2 OperationalTarget concepts.

Task/command target kinds for this milestone:

NONE

HYDRANT

INCIDENT_MAP_OBJECT

INCIDENT_SECTOR

COORDINATE

Do not create a second unrelated target abstraction.

Target data must store:

- target kind,
- canonical entity id where applicable,
- incident relationship where required,
- immutable geometry snapshot at issuance where appropriate,
- optional bounded display-label snapshot.

The canonical entity remains authoritative for identity.

The snapshot is historical evidence of what the commander targeted at
issuance time.

A later entity edit must not rewrite historical task intent.

Do NOT use target geometry to infer command authority.

GEOMETRY DOES NOT GRANT AUTHORITY.

==================================================
9. TARGET VALIDATION
==================================================

At command creation the server must re-resolve and validate the target.

Examples:

HYDRANT
- must be authorized according to the relevant existing read/integration
  rules;
- preserve canonical hydrant UUID.

INCIDENT_MAP_OBJECT
- must belong to the same incident;
- caller must have incident access;
- inactive/invalid target rules must be explicit.

INCIDENT_SECTOR
- same incident;
- valid sector state.

COORDINATE
- finite WGS84 longitude/latitude;
- preserve [longitude, latitude].

For native MOVE_TO / WITHDRAW_TO:

target must resolve to an explicit point.

Do not use polygon/line centroid automatically.

