16. ACKNOWLEDGEMENT AUTHORITY
==================================================

Acknowledgement represents the recipient side.

For INCIDENT_UNIT recipient:

The effective UNIT_LEADER may:

- acknowledge,
- start,
- block,
- complete,
- mark unable

for that unit assignment.

Do not treat descriptive crew role LEADER as UNIT_LEADER authority.

If a unit has no effective UNIT_LEADER, its command may remain ISSUED.

Do not silently let any crew member impersonate the unit leader.

For INCIDENT_CREW_MEMBER recipient:

the matching authenticated user may update their own assignment execution
state while they remain an eligible active incident crew member.

Server must recheck identity and eligibility.

Commanders may CANCEL within their command scope.

Do not let commanders fake recipient acknowledgement.

If an exceptional commander-side administrative status correction is ever
needed, that should be a separate explicitly audited future operation.

